# PlaneWave.Certificate: the plane-wave Galerkin theorems (Lean 4.32.1, Mathlib v4.32.1)

Assembled on 2026-09-20 from the user-confirmed source chain through
milestone 142, including the final correction of each module. Extended in
place on 2026-10-11: every exchange-sector statement carries a particle
labelling `lab`, the tail estimate on the main path uses no exchange symmetry,
milestone 143 adds the spin-inclusive electronic space, milestones 144--149
extend the main theorem to periodic Coulomb systems with quantum particles of
masses at least one and arbitrary charges, fermions and bosons, and static
nuclei, milestone 150 adds their spin-inclusive state space, and milestone
151 bounds the cutoff constants and thresholds by polynomials in the particle
data. The Born--Oppenheimer theorems of milestones 140--143 behind the entry
points are now derived from the Coulomb-system theorems (milestones 149b and
150c), and so are the grid theorems of the grid files, which import this file.
On 2026-10-12 the development files of the manuscript's dynamical results were
merged into this file (Part II, after the entry points of Part I) and into the
grid release file.

## Build

This module is part of the `PlaneWave` library and is compiled by `lake build` (see `README.md`);
it imports only Mathlib. The axiom reports of its sixteen stable entry points, the four
cubic-domain lemmas, the four explicit budget bounds, the six polynomial bounds and the 25 entry
points of Part II are in `AxiomCheck.lean`; each lists only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and
`Quot.sound`.

## Stable entry points (namespace PlaneWaveCertificate)

On the physical electronic space Λ^η(L²(T³) ⊗ ℂ²):

* periodicMolecularCubicError: a ground pair and attained cubic Ritz minima,
  with explicit molecular-data cutoff and error budgets.
* periodicMolecularCubicConvergence: the decreasing sequence of cubic energies,
  its ground-energy limit and infimum, and certified error intervals.
* periodicMolecularCubicAccuracyOfBasisBudget: above the admissible cutoff,
  C_basis <= epsilon*N certifies E <= EN <= E+epsilon.
* periodicMolecularCubicAccuracy: a coarse explicit sufficient integer radius
  for every positive epsilon, using only the molecular-data budgets.

The same four statements in the exchange sector of any particle labelling
lab : Fin eta → ℕ: periodicMolecularSectorCubicError,
periodicMolecularSectorCubicConvergence,
periodicMolecularSectorCubicAccuracyOfBasisBudget and
periodicMolecularSectorCubicAccuracy.

For any periodic Coulomb system sys : CoulombSystem eta ν and any admissible
labelling lab (equal labels only within a species), the same four statements
in the exchange sector of lab, with sign -1 for fermions and +1 for bosons:
periodicCoulombSectorCubicError, periodicCoulombSectorCubicConvergence,
periodicCoulombSectorCubicAccuracyOfBasisBudget and
periodicCoulombSectorCubicAccuracy. Each takes sys and
hlab : sys.IsAdmissible lab, and the first two take lab explicitly. The
Born--Oppenheimer system
CoulombSystem.bo eta data has electrons of mass one and charge -1 and the
clamped nuclei data; at that system the Hamiltonian graph, the sector, the
energy budget, the constants and the threshold are the Born--Oppenheimer ones
(hasCoulombSectorGroundPair_bo, coulombGroundEnergyBudget_bo,
coulombDataCubicThreshold_bo and the other _bo lemmas), and the Sector
statements above are the Coulomb-system statements at that system.

For any periodic Coulomb system and spin multiplicities dim, with dim s spin
states for the species s and 0 < dim s <= D for every species present, the
same four statements on the spin-inclusive space CoulombSpinL2 eta D:
periodicCoulombCubicError, periodicCoulombCubicConvergence,
periodicCoulombCubicAccuracyOfBasisBudget and periodicCoulombCubicAccuracy.
Each takes sys and hdim, and the first two take D and dim explicitly. The
physical states (IsCoulombSpinSector)
change by the exchange sign of the species under simultaneous exchange of
the positions and spins of two particles of one species, and vanish when a
spin value is at or above the multiplicity of its species. At
CoulombSystem.bo eta data with D = 2 and dim = fun _ => 2 these are the
statements on the electronic space above (milestone 150c).

The data-only constants and thresholds of the Error, AccuracyOfBasisBudget and
Accuracy statements are the same for every lab and for the spin-inclusive
spaces.
The Convergence statements use the canonical constants evaluated at the ground
energy E of the space concerned, and prove that a starting radius m0 exists.

Before 2026-10-11 the four periodicMolecular names without Sector stated the
results on the fully antisymmetric spatial sector. Those statements are the
Sector statements with lab = fun _ => 0, for which the condition lab i = lab j
in the sector predicates always holds. The periodicMolecular names without
Sector now state the results on the electronic space.

The entry points at the end of Part I are exact wrappers around the
milestone statements. The milestone declarations they use remain available
for detailed inspection; superseded milestone theorems and the other
declarations that no entry point, cubic-domain lemma, explicit budget bound,
