The auxiliary low-pass mask has been proved redundant for K >= 0 and g >= 0.
Thus the old far/low/high sum is precisely the sum of the unsplit reference
Coulomb operator and the same outer one-body Coulomb term.  At fixed ambient
basis count this operator has no dependence on the truncation cutoff K.

The complex Hermitian condition is proved for the actual kernels and passed
through their exact finite coefficient actions.  Both the potential and the
kinetic-plus-potential Hamiltonian are therefore symmetric without an
independent symmetry hypothesis.

The new end-to-end theorem has neither an arbitrary W argument nor hDecomp or
hWSym.  Its eigenpair and Ritz hypotheses refer to the constructed unsplit
operator.  No estimate is weakened and no numerical constant changes.

The following remain explicit: the specified periodic-remainder essential
bound, the target H2 estimate, the eigenpair/ground/Ritz statements, normalized
antisymmetric coefficients, and the quantitative scale conditions.  The file
still proves a finite-dimensional two-selected-one-body-term specialization,
not the full signed many-electron BO Hamiltonian.  Assembly of all physical
terms and any continuum interpretation must be addressed separately; this is
not hidden in a renamed operator or assumed decomposition.
-/

end

