/-! ## Uniform H2 regularity of normalized finite BO eigenvectors

The already proved H1-to-L2 potential estimate implies an H2 estimate on
every normalized finite eigenvector.  In particular a continuum exhaustion
need not assume a new, uniform H2 bound on its finite Galerkin eigenvectors.
The constant below is deliberately coarse and independent of the basis size.
-/

/-- Explicit uniform H2 norm budget obtained from an absolute energy bound and
an H1-to-L2 multiplier constant. -/
def uniformBOEigenH2Constant (E0 B : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  2 + 8 * E0 + 16 * B ^ 2

lemma uniformBOEigenH2Constant_nonneg {E0 B : ℝ} (hE0 : 0 ≤ E0) :
    0 ≤ uniformBOEigenH2Constant E0 B := by
  unfold uniformBOEigenH2Constant
  positivity

end

