/-! ## Stable release interface

These wrappers repeat the exact compiled statements under permanent names.
They introduce no new assumptions or mathematical proof steps.

The four main entry points are stated on the physical electronic space
`Λ^η(L²(T³) ⊗ ℂ²)` of the manuscript: spin-dependent wavefunctions that are
antisymmetric under simultaneous exchange of the positions and spins of two
electrons. The four `Sector` entry points give the same statements in the
exchange sector of any particle labelling `lab`. The constant labelling is the
fully antisymmetric spatial sector, that is, the fully spin-polarised states.

The four `periodicCoulombSector` entry points give the same statements for any
periodic Coulomb system `sys` (quantum particles with masses at least one,
charges and species, each species fermionic or bosonic, and static nuclei), in
the exchange sector of any admissible labelling `lab`. The four
Born--Oppenheimer `Sector` statements above are their instances at
`CoulombSystem.bo eta data` (milestone 149b).

The four `periodicCoulomb` entry points without `Sector` give the same
statements on the spin-inclusive space `L²((T³)^η; ⊗_a ℂ^{d_a})` of a Coulomb
system, written in spin components (`CoulombSpinL2 eta D`), with `dim s` spin
states for the species `s`. The four main Born--Oppenheimer entry points are
their instances at `CoulombSystem.bo eta data` with `D = 2` and
`dim = fun _ => 2` (milestone 150c).
-/

